        <body>
            <div xml:id="toc">

                <pb facs="0009" n="V" xml:id="pgV"/>

                <head>CONTENTS</head>
                <list>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pgIII">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preface</hi>
                        </ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>Participation by the United States in the work of the European Advisory
                        Commission: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg1">I. Organization and scope of activity of the
                                    European Advisory Commission; question of civil affairs
                                    arrangements for liberated areas</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg39">II. The preparation of surrender terms for
                                    Hungary, Rumania, Bulgaria, and Finland</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg40">III. Consultation by the Commission with
                                    European Allied countries</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg85">IV. Admission of France to full membership in
                                    the Commission</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg100">V. Questions of terms of surrender, zones of
                                    occupation, and control machinery for Germany</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg434">VI. Questions of zones of occupation and
                                    control machinery for Austria</ref>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg484">Consideration of the application of “unconditional
                            surrender” terms to Germany; unofficial peace feelers from Germany</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg580">Application of the principle of unconditional surrender
                            to Bulgaria, Hungary, and Rumania</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>Preliminaries to the establishment of an international organization for
                        the maintenance of international peace and security: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg614">I. Arrangements for exploratory discussions on
                                    world security organization</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>II. Dumbarton Oaks Conversations: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg713">A. Anglo-American-Soviet phase: August
                                            21–September 28, 1944</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg850">B. Anglo-American-Chinese phase:
                                            September 29–October 7, 1944</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg901">III. Continuing preparations for a Conference
                                    of United Nations</ref>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg924">Interest of the United States in the reaction of
                            non-participating Governments to the Dumbarton Oaks Proposals</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg960">Attitude of the United States regarding the eligibility
                            of the Vatican for membership in the proposed international
                            organization</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg965">Participation of United States in the Conference of
                            Allied Ministers of Education, London, April 5–29, 1944, and the
                            proposed establishment of a United Nations organization for educational
                            and cultural reconstruction</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg981">Governmental assistance to persons forced to emigrate
                            for political or racial reasons</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1192">Emergency measures for the welfare and repatriation of
                            American citizens in enemy, former enemy, and enemy-occupied
                            countries</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1227">Allied declarations and warnings regarding Nazi
                            atrocities</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1265">Discussions regarding procedures and scope of the
                            United Nations Commission for the Investigation of War Crimes</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1410">Representations to neutral governments against the
                            granting of asylum to persons guilty of war crimes</ref>
                    </item>
                    <pb facs="0010" n="VI" xml:id="pgVI"/>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1455">Successful Anglo-American effort to effect Soviet
                            participation in the work of the London Political Warfare Coordinating
                            Committee</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1466">Establishment of the State–War–Navy Coordinating
                            Committee</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1471">Policy of the United States with respect to diplomatic
                            and consular property of enemy governments and the property of enemy
                            diplomatic and consular personnel in liberated areas</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1507">Policy and attitude of the Department of State with
                            regard to censorship</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1525">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Appendix</hi>: Reorganization of the
                            Department of State</ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1529">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Index</hi>
                        </ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maps</hi>: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg152">Germany—Zones of Occupation <hi
                                        rendition="#italic">facing</hi>
                                </ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg196">Proposals for the Occupation of Germany <hi
                                        rendition="#italic">facing</hi>
                                </ref>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                </list>
